 "_about": "Jeremiah Curtin's folk tales and myths, as he took them down and put them into English: Myths and Folk Tales of Ireland (the Gutenberg file is from Dover's 1975 reprint of Myths and Folk-Lore of Ireland, Boston, 1890, which leaves out the original introduction, frontispiece and dedication), Myths and Folk-tales of the Russians, Western Slavs, and Magyars (copyright 1890), Hero-Tales of Ireland (1894), Creation Myths of Primitive America (copyright 1898), Seneca Fiction, Legends, and Myths (with J. N. B. Hewitt, in the Bureau of American Ethnology's Thirty-Second Annual Report, 1910-1911, printed 1918) and Myths of the Modocs (London: Sampson Low, 1912, per Gutenberg's record). His Sienkiewicz translations are on lane C's curtin shelf; his histories of the Mongols are not taken. Added at the coordinator's standing relay (2026-10-02/03: choose public-domain storytellers batches; Adam may veto).",
